&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;font-display font-bold text-[19px] mt-5 mb-1.5&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed mb-2&quot;&gt;When a customer pushes a change, they need their CI/CD jobs to start quickly and run reliably, even when demand spikes. You&#39;ll help make that happen on GitLab.com by improving how Hosted Runners provision compute, isolate customer workloads, and recover from failures. Your decisions will shape how long customers wait for jobs to start and how efficiently GitLab uses cloud compute.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed mb-2&quot;&gt;As a Senior Staff Site Reliability Engineer, you&#39;ll set technical direction across teams while continuing to write and operate production software in Go. You&#39;ll lead work across the runner control plane, worker provisioning, and job execution. Your primary focus will be GitLab.com, and you&#39;ll also provide technical leadership support for GitLab Dedicated Hosted Runners. You&#39;ll report to the engineering manager responsible for Hosted Runners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;text-[15px] mb-1 font-semibold&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Some examples of our projects:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;space-y-1.5 ml-4&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Tuning autoscaling to reduce job wait times during demand spikes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Evaluating ways to isolate customer workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Improving how runner usage is measured for capacity planning and billing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;font-display font-bold text-[19px] mt-5 mb-1.5&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;space-y-1.5 ml-4&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Lead architecture and delivery across teams. Plan migrations with representative workload tests, safe capacity handovers, and rollback paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Write, review, and ship Go code across GitLab Runner, autoscaling components, cloud integrations, and operational tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Improve reliability from job pickup through cleanup. Join the Runners Platform on-call rotation, investigate failures across system layers, and verify fixes in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Work with Security and Runner engineers to evaluate workload isolation, balancing security and compatibility with performance and cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Build observability that connects the customer experience with fleet behavior and guides capacity decisions. Partner with Finance, Product, and the billing platform team on usage metering and cost attribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Reduce recurring operational work through automation, tooling, and runbooks that engineers can use independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Mentor experienced engineers through design, implementation, and operations. Clarify ownership across teams and help engineers validate AI-assisted changes before they reach production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;font-display font-bold text-[19px] mt-5 mb-1.5&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;space-y-1.5 ml-4&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Recent hands-on experience building and operating production systems software such as controllers, agents, or schedulers. You&#39;ve personally shipped code that handles challenges such as concurrency, retries, or resource cleanup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Strong programming skills in Go or another systems language, with the ability to become productive in Go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Deep Linux and networking knowledge. You can trace production failures across system layers and use measurements to validate fixes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Experience operating Kubernetes in production, including diagnosing scheduling and resource issues and managing rollouts and recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;Experience building or operating autoscaled or dynamically scheduled compute, such as VM fleets, serverless platforms, or batch systems. You bring experience with public cloud and infrastructure automation or comparable fleet operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;A working understanding of the CI job lifecycle and the implications of running customer-controlled code. You can bring that knowledge from outside a CI/CD team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed&quot;&gt;A record of leading technical initiatives across teams and personally contributing to implementation through production. You build agreement through clear writing and asynchronous collaboration, and mentor engineers to own what they build and operate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;font-display font-bold text-[19px] mt-5 mb-1.5&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;text-[15px] leading-relaxed mb-2&quot;&gt;Hosted Runners operates the compute behind customers&#39; CI/CD jobs. You&#39;ll work with Runner Core to turn lessons from operating the fleet into improvements to the open-source GitLab Runner. You&#39;ll also work with Product and partner teams to agree on priorities and ownership for shared changes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;text-[15px] mb-1 font-semibold&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn more:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ml-4 space-y-1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;text-[15px] font-medium&quot; href=&quot;https://docs.gitlab.com/administration/dedicated/hosted_runners/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Hosted runners for GitLab Dedicated (docs)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The base salary range for this role’s listed level is currently for residents of the&amp;nbsp;United States only. This range is intended to reflect the role&#39;s base salary rate in locations throughout the US.&amp;nbsp;Grade level and salary ranges are determined through interviews and a review of education, experience, knowledge, skills, abilities of the applicant, equity with other team members, alignment with market data,&amp;nbsp;and geographic location.&amp;nbsp;The base salary range does not include any bonuses, equity, or benefits. See more information on our &lt;a class=&quot;waffle-rich-text-link&quot; href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-link=&quot;https://bit.ly/GLBeneUS&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#1155cc;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:underline;font-family:&#39;&#39;Arial&#39;&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt;benefits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:none;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;waffle-rich-text-link&quot; href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/stock-options/&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-link=&quot;https://bit.ly/GLequity&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#1155cc;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:underline;font-family:&#39;&#39;Arial&#39;&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt;equity&lt;/a&gt;. Sales roles are also eligible for incentive pay targeted at up to 100% of the offered base salary.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;United States Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$184,800&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$314,400 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Figma is growing our team of passionate creatives and builders on a mission to make design accessible to all. Figma’s platform helps teams bring ideas to life—whether you&#39;re brainstorming, creating a prototype, translating designs into code, or iterating with AI. From idea to product, Figma empowers teams to streamline workflows, move faster, and work together in real time from anywhere in the world. If you&#39;re excited to shape the future of design and collaboration, join us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We’re building the next chapter of AI-native craft and creativity - where craft and technology meet. Our unified platform bridges the gap between AI capabilities and human creativity, and lets professional creatives and designers harness the power of the world’s leading AI models without losing precision, expression, or soul. Together, we’re building tools that help people move faster without sacrificing quality, precision, or craft - a platform where AI supports creativity instead of flattening it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a scrappy, hands-on AI Product Technical Program Manager to join Figma Weave as the team’s first TPM. You’ll partner with Engineering, Product, and Design to turn ambiguous customer needs and new AI capabilities into reliable creative workflows. You’ll lead programs across the AI model lifecycle, usage economics, and products like the Weave API. You’ll get close to the architecture, help teams make informed technical tradeoffs, and stay accountable through launch and adoption. You’ll also build AI workflows and automation yourself to help the team move faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;This full-time role can be based in our New York hub or remotely on the East Coast of the United States. You’ll join a team spread across the United States, Europe, and Tel Aviv, with occasional travel to work alongside Figma Weave partners in Tel Aviv.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do at Figma Weave:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead model lifecycle management across image, video, editing, enhancement, audio/lip-sync, 3D, and vector models, using the existing evaluation process to drive new model integration, launch, updates, and deprecation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make tradeoffs around quality, reliability, latency, cost, and capacity clear to the decision owners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track model limitations, integration issues, and provider dependencies through fixes, rollout, and follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Engineering, Partnerships, and Finance on provider agreements, quotas, rate limits, and capacity commitments so Weave can support product growth and launch demand. Bring in Product, Legal, and Security to resolve dependencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage AI costs, capacity, and unit economics across 10+ providers and 50+ models. Forecast usage and spend, plan provider capacity for launches, and work with engineers on fallback options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build things that make work less work. Improve process design and build AI workflows and automation that help the team move faster. Use APIs, scripts, or data queries to improve program visibility, streamline processes, and remove recurring bottlenecks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead horizontal product programs that span Weave teams, such as the Weave API. Understand how API contracts, authentication, permissions, asynchronous execution, and usage limits affect delivery. Coordinate dependencies across Weave and Figma, work through technical blockers, and follow the program through testing, release, and adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional technical readiness for Config and other major launches. Work with engineering leads on end-to-end workflow testing, provider capacity, monitoring, and rollback plans. Bring together Support, Legal, Marketing, and other launch partners, make risks and go/no-go decisions clear, and follow through on customer issues and incident action items after release&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’d love to hear from you if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scrappiness and adaptability: You get into the details and take practical steps to move work forward. You can investigate a problem, partner with your engineering counterparts on a solution, or build a quick prototype without waiting for a perfect plan. You adjust when priorities change and follow through on what you start&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Third-party AI model integration: You’ve led programs that bring third-party AI models into a product and keep them working. You can use evaluation findings and usage data to drive decisions across Engineering, Product, and Partnerships, including tradeoffs around quality, reliability, latency, cost, capacity, and unit economics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-enabled process design and automation: Hands-on experience building lightweight processes by leveraging AI workflows, automation, or internal tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical judgment and hands-on problem solving: You can follow a workflow from the user interface through backend services and external model APIs. You reason about latency, throughput, rate limits, retries, and failure modes with engineers. You’ve managed AI cost structures, including usage and spend, pricing negotiations, and capacity planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI product program delivery and ownership: You’ve led customer-facing technical programs with cross-functional partners, from an ambiguous need through launch and adoption. You judge success by whether the product works for customers and delivers the intended result&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;While it’s not required, it’s an added plus if you also have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve been an early TPM or worked at a startup, where you helped engineering teams plan and ship without adding more process than they needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve worked with a broad set of model providers, including early-access programs or model migrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI research or applied AI program experience is preferred. You’ve partnered with researchers and engineers and used their findings to bring new capabilities into a product. Experience with generative image or video products, and how creative users judge output quality, is especially useful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Figma, one of our values is Grow as you go. We believe in hiring smart, curious people who are excited to learn and develop their skills. If you’re excited about this role but your past experience doesn’t align perfectly with the points outlined in the job description, we encourage you to apply anyways. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Pay Transparency Disclosure&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Job level and actual compensation will be decided based on factors including, but not limited to, individual qualifications objectively assessed during the interview process (including skills and prior relevant experience, potential impact, and scope of role), market demands, and specific work location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Figma offers equity to employees, as well as a competitive package of additional benefits, including health, dental, and vision coverage; retirement benefits with company contributions; parental leave and reproductive or family planning support; mental health and wellness benefits; and paid time off. Figma provides paid sick leave, holidays, and other leave benefits in compliance with applicable federal, state, and local laws, including the requirements of the Washington Minimum Wage Act and related regulations. Exempt employees are eligible for employer‑provided paid flexible PTO in addition to flexible paid sick leave. PTO is subject to manager approval. Additional benefits may include company recharge days, cell phone and home internet reimbursements, and a number of lifestyle spending accounts. Figma also offers sales incentive compensation for most sales roles and an annual bonus plan for eligible non-sales roles. All compensation and benefits are subject to applicable plan terms and may be modified by Figma at any time, consistent with applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Base Salary Range:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$185,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$269,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Figma we celebrate and support our differences. We know employing a team rich in diverse thoughts, experiences, and opinions allows our employees, our product and our community to flourish. Figma is an &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2022-10/EEOC_KnowYourRights_screen_reader_10_20.pdf&quot;&gt;equal opportunity workplace&lt;/a&gt; - we are dedicated to equal employment opportunities regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity/expression, veteran status&lt;strong&gt;, &lt;/strong&gt;or any other characteristic protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We will work to ensure individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to apply for a role, participate in the interview process, perform essential job functions, and receive other benefits and privileges of employment. If you require accommodation, please reach out to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:accommodations-ext@figma.com&quot;&gt;accommodations-ext@figma.com&lt;/a&gt;. These modifications enable an individual with a disability to have an equal opportunity not only to get a job, but successfully perform their job tasks to the same extent as people without disabilities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Examples of accommodations include but are not limited to:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Holding interviews in an accessible location&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enabling closed captioning on video conferencing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring all written communication be compatible with screen readers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Changing the mode or format of interviews&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To ensure the integrity of our hiring process and facilitate a more personal connection, we require all candidates keep their cameras on during video interviews. Additionally, if hired you will be required to attend in person onboarding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By applying for this job, the candidate acknowledges and agrees that any personal data contained in their application or supporting materials will be processed in accordance with &lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;https://www.figma.com/legal/candidate-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.figma.com/legal/candidate-privacy-notice/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Figma&#39;s Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application limits:&lt;/strong&gt; To help candidates focus on the opportunities most relevant to their skills and experience, Figma limits the number and frequency of applications. These limits apply to all roles:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidates may submit up to 5 applications during any rolling 30-day period.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidates may not reapply to the same role while an application is active or within 90 days of receiving a rejection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Once the applicable days has passed, candidates are welcome to apply again.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Zscaler (NASDAQ: ZS) accelerates digital transformation so customers can be more agile, efficient, resilient, and secure. The Zscaler Zero Trust Exchange platform protects thousands of customers from cyberattacks and data loss by securely connecting users, devices, and applications in any location. Distributed across 200+ public data centers globally and thousands of private sites at the edge, the SASE-based Zero Trust Exchange is the world’s largest in-line cloud security platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe the future of work is Human + AI and are building an AI-native enterprise where human potential is amplified by machine intelligence to solve the world’s hardest security challenges. Driven by deep customer obsession, we are committed to the mission, outcome, and to each other. We bring these commitments to life through three core behaviors: ownership and collaboration, trust through outcomes and impact, and a challenge culture with ongoing feedback. Ready to make an impact at the company pioneering security transformation in the AI era? Join us at Zscaler.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are looking for a Principal Site Reliability Engineer to join our team. This is a hybrid role going into the Santa Clara, CA office 3 days a week or Remote (US) role, reporting to the Senior Manager, Cloud Operations in the Infrastructure services and architecture team. As a lead engineer, you will leverage deep expertise in IaC/CaC, Linux virtualization, and physical hardware management to drive our infrastructure forward. You will oversee networking services and general software engineering to ensure our systems remain scalable, resilient, and high-performing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do (Role Expectations)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor other engineers and lead high-impact infrastructure projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support business operations by responding to alerts and triaging systems to restore mission-critical capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the reliability and performance of all customer-facing services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, document, and build technical solutions that align with evolving organizational needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Agile processes to maintain high velocity and a collaborative environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are (Success Profile)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in ambiguity, comfortably building the path forward in a dynamic environment where you see uncertainty as an opportunity to build something meaningful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You act like an owner with a strong bias for action and deep integrity, seamlessly navigating between high-level strategy and hands-on execution to drive outstanding outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
